# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` into the SDK stage, so whatever survives this file gets built
# on top of. Host build output is the dangerous part: obj/ carries staticwebassets.build.json
# with absolute host paths (C:\Users\...\ on Windows) plus a prebuilt scoped-CSS bundle, and
# MSBuild treats those as up to date rather than regenerating them for linux-x64. The result is
# an image whose DokkanDaily.styles.css does not match the scope IDs on the rendered markup, so
# every CSS-isolation rule silently stops matching. CI never hit this because actions/checkout
# hands the deploy job a clean tree.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/publish/
**/TestResults/

# Source control and CI - nothing in the build reads these
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# IDE and editor state
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Docker's own files are passed with -f, not read from the context
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Database build artifacts (the DB image builds from src/DokkanDailyDB with its own context)
Dacpac/
**/*.dacpac
